  "summary": "Jewish paper cutting is a traditional form of Jewish folk art made by cutting figures and sentences in paper or parchment.",
  "description": "Jewish paper cutting is a traditional form of Jewish folk art made by cutting figures and sentences in paper or parchment.\n\nIt is connected with various customs and ceremonies, and associated with holidays and family life. Paper cuts often decorated ketubbot (marriage contracts), Mizrahs, and ornaments for festive occasions. Paper cutting was practiced by Jewish communities in both Eastern Europe and North Africa and the Middle East for centuries and has seen a revival in modern times in Israel and elsewhere.",
